00:16:00,627 --> 00:16:01,801
effect on history."

207
00:16:04,141 --> 00:16:09,159
Answer out loud before you open the answers
file. A strong answer splits the pull

208
00:16:09,199 --> 00:16:12,843
into its two steps and places
the stop exactly at the seam.

209
00:16:12,883 --> 00:16:17,839
It lists what moved and what did not in
terms of refs, the index and the working

210
00:16:17,879 --> 00:16:18,151
tree.

211
00:16:18,491 --> 00:16:23,212
It names the three answers by flag and by
configuration key, and for each describes

212
00:16:23,252 --> 00:16:27,744
the resulting history in one phrase: what
is created, what is replaced, what is

213
00:16:27,784 --> 00:16:32,334
refused. A senior answer adds which one
it would set globally and where it would

214
00:16:32,374 --> 00:16:34,227
never let a pull create a commit.

215
00:16:36,067 --> 00:16:38,994
Let's land this. You
should now be able to say:

216
00:16:39,334 --> 00:16:44,852
The upstream of a branch is two configuration
values, a remote and the server's ref

217
00:16:44,892 --> 00:16:48,670
name, and @{u} resolves them
to a remote-tracking branch.

218
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:54,027
Under push.default=simple, a bare git push
goes to the upstream only if its name

219
00:16:54,067 --> 00:16:57,175
equals the branch's name.
Otherwise it refuses.

220
00:16:57,515 --> 00:17:00,621
git pull is a fetch followed
by one integration step.

221
00:17:00,661 --> 00:17:05,370
When the branches have diverged and nothing
is configured, the fetch has already

222
00:17:05,410 --> 00:17:10,297
happened and Git stops before integrating.
The three answers are fast-forward only,

223
00:17:10,337 --> 00:17:14,394
merge and rebase, and a flag on the
command line beats configuration.

224
00:17:16,234 --> 00:17:20,127
Read sections 12.5 and 12.6 of Chapter 12.

225
00:17:20,467 --> 00:17:25,233
Today you found the seam in git pull:
a fetch that can't hurt you, then one

226
00:17:25,273 --> 00:17:30,488
integration step that you choose. That
Monday-morning message is Git asking a fair

227
00:17:30,528 --> 00:17:34,461
question. Do Lab 7.3 while this
is fresh. Next time: git push.

228
00:17:34,501 --> 00:17:37,793
Until then, look at the
state first and type second.

229
00:17:37,833 --> 00:17:39,331
See you in the next one.
